  "text": "Fairy lover, the fairy mistress, is an Irish, Scottish, and Breton figure. The lianan sidhe, she is also the spirit the bards knew. She carried off the greatest poet or the fairest mortal male. Her grace made the loveliest woman seem plain. She called her mate through his dreams until he came to her. He found her on a charmed island in the west or under an old mound. Time passed by differently in her land. A single night there could cross a century here. The poet Oisín was taken by Niamh of the Golden Hair. He fell from his horse and turned to dust at once. Some fairy women left their human husbands and they pined away. Aine of Lough Gur appears in both the lover and the death parts. Keats used her shape for his poem.",
